---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import CausalDiagram from '../../components/diagrams/CausalDiagram.astro';
import studyDesign from '../../assets/figures/bikelane-study-design.png';
import eventStudy from '../../assets/figures/bikelane-event-study.png';
import geographyPlacebo from '../../assets/figures/bikelane-geography-placebo.png';
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Protected bike lanes & Divvy ridership"
  summary="A causal study of whether newly completed protected bike-lane corridors changed monthly Divvy trip starts at nearby stations. The design was locked before any treatment effect was read, and the checks it failed are still in the write-up."
  metaDescription="A causal study by Quoc Nguyen of protected bike lanes and Divvy ridership: matched group-time ATT, pre-registered gates, 16 robustness specifications, and 50 geography placebos."
  stack={['Python', 'pandas', 'GeoPandas', 'statsmodels', 'SciPy', 'Matplotlib', 'Pytest', 'Make']}
  nextSteps={[
    'Replace the medium-confidence first-verified treatment dates with permit or construction records — shifting conservative dates one month earlier is currently enough to move the interval off zero, and that fragility is the weakest part of the design.',
    'Extend the placebo inventory from a concurrent-project proxy to a complete registry of Chicago transport projects, so the geography tail criterion is tested against real alternatives rather than an approximation of them.',
    'Source monthly station coordinates so relocations inside the panel can be reconstructed instead of assumed away.',
  ]}
  draft={false}
>
  <Fragment slot="links">
    <a
      href="https://github.com/koshiroquoc/bikelane-causal"
      class="u-link font-mono text-[13px] tracking-[0.04em] text-accent"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noreferrer"
    >
      repo ↗
    </a>
    <span class="font-mono text-[13px] tracking-[0.04em] text-muted">
      release v1.0.0 · make reproduce
    </span>
    <span class="font-mono text-[13px] tracking-[0.04em] text-muted">
      panel from
      <a href="/projects/bikeshare-forecast" class="u-link text-accent">Divvy forecasting ↗</a>
    </span>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="problem">
    <p>
      Cities justify protected bike lanes with before-and-after counts on the corridor
      itself. That comparison cannot separate the lane from everything else that changed
      that season — weather, a new station, a citywide ridership trend — so the number it
      produces is not an effect, it is a coincidence with a date attached.
    </p>
    <p>
      Divvy publishes station-level trips monthly, and Chicago publishes when each bikeway
      was completed. Together they allow a staggered-adoption design: stations near a newly
      protected corridor become treated at different times, and stations that never got one
      supply the counterfactual.
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted">
      The second problem is harder than the statistics, and it is the one this project is
      actually built around. Whoever runs the analysis chooses the radius, the control
      pool, the estimator and the robustness checks — and can choose them after seeing
      which combination gives the cleanest story. So the design, the thresholds, the
      estimator roles and the change-control rules were written down and locked before any
      treatment effect was read, and the repository records what was allowed to be claimed
      afterwards.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="diagram"><CausalDiagram /></Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="diagram-caption">
    Fig. 02 — A locked corridor inventory and the Divvy station panel become a matched
    station-month panel; each phase must clear its gate before the next one runs, and the
    final claim is checked against a machine-readable contract.
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="evaluation">
    <div class="max-w-[60ch]">
      <span class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.08em] uppercase text-muted">Measured</span>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink">
        The change in monthly trip starts at stations within 300 m of a newly protected
        corridor, relative to matched stations that never received one. Reported as a
        percentage of the estimated treated counterfactual mean, with member and casual
        trips split out as a secondary outcome.
      </p>
      <span class="mt-8 block font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.08em] uppercase text-muted">
        Eval design
      </span>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted">
        12 corridors, 40 treated stations, and 120 cohort-local control assignments drawn
        from 83 unique control stations — three per treated station, matched without
        replacement on pre-treatment level, slope, variability and member share only. No
        post-treatment outcome enters matching. The panel runs July 2023 to June 2026 with a
        complete 12-month pre and post period for every station-cohort. Uncertainty is
        two-way clustered by treated corridor and reused control station, with t critical
        values on 11 corridor degrees of freedom rather than station counts.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted">
        Five estimators were registered in advance with fixed roles. Two are transparency
        baselines that were never eligible to be the headline; one is the primary; one is a
        conditional magnitude check; one is a required specific-date sensitivity. The
        selection rule was written before the estimates existed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 grid max-w-[720px] grid-cols-1 gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3 sm:gap-4">
      <div>
        <div class="font-mono text-[30px] leading-none font-medium text-ink">−10.8%</div>
        <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">
          Primary ATT · 95% CI −24.0 to +2.3
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="font-mono text-[30px] leading-none font-medium text-ink">16</div>
        <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">
          Pre-locked robustness specs
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="font-mono text-[30px] leading-none font-medium text-ink">0.235</div>
        <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">
          Geography placebo tail · locked at 0.10
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-12 m-0 max-w-[860px]">
      <Image
        src={studyDesign}
        alt="Map of Chicago showing the 12 treated bike-lane corridors, the 40 treated Divvy stations within 300 m, and the matched control stations."
        widths={[640, 860]}
        sizes="(min-width: 900px) 860px, 100vw"
        class="h-auto w-full rounded-xl border border-grid"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <figcaption class="mt-3 max-w-[80ch] font-mono text-[13px] tracking-[0.05em] text-muted">
        Fig. 03a — Study design: treated corridors, the stations inside the 300 m buffer, and
        the matched controls that supply the counterfactual.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-12 max-w-[860px] overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[620px] border-collapse text-left">
        <caption class="caption mb-4 text-left text-muted">
          Pre-registered estimator registry
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <th
              class="py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted"
            >
              Estimator
            </th>
            <th
              class="py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted"
            >
              Role
            </th>
            <th
              class="py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted"
            >
              Effect
            </th>
            <th
              class="py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted"
            >
              95% interval
            </th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="font-mono text-[13px] text-ink">
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-accent">group-time ATT</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">primary</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">−10.8%</td>
            <td class="py-3">[−24.0%, 2.3%]</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">cohort-stacked PPML</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">conditional magnitude</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">−4.8%</td>
            <td class="py-3 text-muted">[−18.6%, 11.2%]</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">group-time ATT · specific dates</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">required sensitivity</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">−11.0%</td>
            <td class="py-3 text-muted">[−34.7%, 12.7%]</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">pooled PPML TWFE</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">transparency only</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">−4.3%</td>
            <td class="py-3 text-muted">[−10.4%, 2.2%]</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">TWFE OLS log1p</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">transparency only</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">−1.6%</td>
            <td class="py-3 text-muted">[−8.9%, 6.2%]</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 max-w-[60ch]">
      <p class="text-muted">
        PPML was not promoted despite being the more favourable-looking magnitude. Cohort
        effects are severely heterogeneous — a 61.8 percentage-point range — and two cohorts
        contain a single treated corridor, which makes few-cluster inference unreliable and
        made PPML ineligible under the locked rule. The two samples reconcile and their
        intervals overlap, so the choice was not a judgement call about which number to
        prefer.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-12 m-0 max-w-[860px]">
      <Image
        src={eventStudy}
        alt="Event-study plot of the matched group-time ATT by month relative to corridor completion, with 95% confidence bands spanning zero after treatment."
        widths={[640, 860]}
        sizes="(min-width: 900px) 860px, 100vw"
        class="h-auto w-full rounded-xl border border-grid"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <figcaption class="mt-3 max-w-[80ch] font-mono text-[13px] tracking-[0.05em] text-muted">
        Fig. 03b — Event study. The post-treatment path sits below zero but its bands include
        it throughout; the pre-treatment leads are the reason the interpretation stays
        narrow.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-12 max-w-[860px] overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[620px] border-collapse text-left">
        <caption class="caption mb-4 text-left text-muted">
          Robustness and falsification — 16 specifications
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <th
              class="py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted"
            >
              Check
            </th>
            <th
              class="py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted"
            >
              Result
            </th>
            <th
              class="py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted"
            >
              Reading
            </th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="font-mono text-[13px] text-ink">
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Treated / donut radii</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">−10.7% to −12.1%</td>
            <td class="py-3 text-muted">stable</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Drop first 1–2 post months</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">−11.2%, −12.1%</td>
            <td class="py-3 text-muted">stable</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">New protected lanes only</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">−8.6% [−25.6%, 8.4%]</td>
            <td class="py-3 text-muted">stable, less precise</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Member / casual outcomes</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">−12.7% / −6.9%</td>
            <td class="py-3 text-muted">stable</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Leave one corridor out</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">−15.0% to −5.8%</td>
            <td class="py-3 text-muted">one influential corridor</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Conservative dates ±1 month</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">−14.5% to −8.6%</td>
            <td class="py-3 text-point">−1 month moves the CI off zero</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Timing placebo, 6 months early</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">+2.4% [−5.1%, 10.0%]</td>
            <td class="py-3 text-muted">clears — no spurious effect</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">50 matched geography placebos</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">median +3.2%, tail p = 0.235</td>
            <td class="py-3 text-point">fails the locked 0.10 criterion</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-12 m-0 max-w-[860px]">
      <Image
        src={geographyPlacebo}
        alt="Distribution of 50 matched geography-placebo estimates with the real estimate marked on the negative side of the distribution but inside its tail."
        widths={[640, 860]}
        sizes="(min-width: 900px) 860px, 100vw"
        class="h-auto w-full rounded-xl border border-grid"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <figcaption class="mt-3 max-w-[80ch] font-mono text-[13px] tracking-[0.05em] text-muted">
        Fig. 03c — 50 fixed-seed placebo corridors drawn from streets with no protected
        segment. The real estimate sits outside the central 90% interval, but not far enough
        into the tail to clear the criterion set in advance.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-12 max-w-[60ch]">
      <span class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.08em] uppercase text-muted">
        What failed → what was kept
      </span>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted">
        Two checks did not clear, and both survive into the conclusion rather than being
        tuned away. The four-bin pre-treatment placebo-lead test rejects exact zero,
        <span class="font-mono text-[13px] text-ink">F(4,11) = 4.41, p = 0.023</span> — so
        parallel trends cannot be assumed, though the largest single lead, −16.3%, stays
        under the 20% automatic-failure threshold that was fixed in advance. And the
        geography placebo returns an empirical two-sided tail probability of 0.235 against a
        locked threshold of 0.10, which means an estimate this large is reachable by drawing
        a random unprotected street.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted">
        Either failure alone is enough to block a clean causal claim, so Phase 5 exits as
        <span class="font-mono text-[13px] text-ink">PASS WITH LIMITATIONS</span> instead of
        being re-specified until it passes. The fix that would actually help is better
        treatment-date provenance, not a different estimator.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 max-w-[60ch] border-l border-accent pl-6">
      <span class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.08em] uppercase text-muted">
        Claims contract
      </span>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink">
        The release records one sentence as the only conclusion the evidence supports, and a
        test fails if the write-up drifts from it:
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-[13px] leading-[1.7] text-muted">
        "The analysis does not establish an increase in nearby monthly Divvy trip starts;
        identification and geography-placebo limitations preclude a clean causal claim."
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted">
        It also does not support the opposite reading. A negative point estimate with an
        interval crossing zero, a pre-trend warning and a soft placebo tail is not evidence
        that lanes reduced ridership — and the contract exists so that a tidier version of
        this project cannot be told later.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</ProjectLayout>
